## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over partitioning with a quadratic segment cost, requiring prefix sums, base cases, and reconstruction, plus discussion of optimizations.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions: dp[i][t] for first i elements into t segments
- Prefix sums for O(1) segment sums
- Quadratic segment cost and optimization (CHT or Divide-and-Conquer)
- Reconstructing segment boundaries with a prev table
- Time/space trade-offs and edge cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const S = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) S[i] = S[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const INF = 1e18;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const prev = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k && t <= i; t++) {
      for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        const diff = S[i] - S[j];
        const cost = diff * diff;
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + cost;
        if (val < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          prev[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return { cost: dp[n][k] };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a DP over partitioned subarrays with a non-standard per-subarray score and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP on non-overlapping subarrays
- Prefix sums and range minimums
- Path reconstruction and base cases
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScore(A, k){
  const n = A.length; const P=[0]; for(let i=0;i<n;i++) P[i+1]=P[i]+A[i];
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1]=P[i]-Math.min(...A.slice(0,i));
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const minVal=Math.min(...A.slice(p,i));
        const val=dp[p][t-1]+(P[i]-P[p])-minVal;
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; prev[i][t]=p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would trace back using prev
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

